subjective -- that's the breaks.  I tend to be on the lenient side,
actually, in that I'll give the benefit of the doubt to the offender.
At least the first time.  Recidivism is "frowned" upon.

Being at an educational institution, I believe it's pretty much
"anything goes" -- within reason.  Things like massive postings
(cross-posted or not), chain letters, things of that sort are not
looked upon kindly.  (Some are clearly against network policy, which we
are obliged to uphold.  Others are just plain stupid, so the user has
to be "educated" -- this _is_ a university, after all.:-))

