We haven't had to delve into it deeper.  But I believe the INTERNET policy
can be interpreted as one which research and education is its intent.

In fact, It is my impression that the Usenet thing is really borderline
if you take a conservative approach. 

I've been asking for a copy from our regional manager (internet manager),
but it hasn't been a high priority.

I would say, you should find out who your regional INTERNET manager
is and ask him/her to get you a copy.  Even if it is old, it would
be a very good place to start.


And personally, I believe people do have a right to express themselves,
but they do not have the right to attack others.


My rule of thumb is if I get messages from sysadmins then I do something.
If I get several messages from users I do something.
If I get a VERY strong letter from an individual I do something.

Other than that, I usually send email to the local person and ask
what the deal is......
